[{"id":29,"date":"2026-07-10T05:24:01","date_gmt":"2026-07-10T05:24:01","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/admin.rdtvideodownloader.com\/?p=29"},"modified":"2026-07-10T05:24:03","modified_gmt":"2026-07-10T05:24:03","slug":"how-to-download-reddit-gifs-as-mp4","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/admin.rdtvideodownloader.com\/how-to-download-reddit-gifs-as-mp4\/","title":{"rendered":"How to Download Reddit GIFs as MP4 \u2014 Free Tool, No App Needed"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">If you&#8217;ve spent any decent amount of time on Reddit, you know that GIFs are basically their own language. A perfectly timed reaction GIF, a satisfying slow-motion clip, a looping moment of pure chaos from r\/Whatcouldgowrong \u2014 these things are <em>gold<\/em>.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">But saving them? That&#8217;s where it gets annoying.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">When you try to download a GIF from Reddit, one of three things usually happens:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Nothing downloads at all<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>You get a broken file that won&#8217;t open<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>You get a massive, low-quality .gif file that takes up way too much storage<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here&#8217;s the thing most people don&#8217;t realize: <strong>Reddit GIFs aren&#8217;t actually GIFs anymore.<\/strong> They haven&#8217;t been for years. Reddit automatically converts all GIF uploads into MP4 video files behind the scenes \u2014 which is why they loop smoothly, load fast, and look sharp in the Reddit player.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">So the smartest move isn&#8217;t to save them as GIF files. It&#8217;s to download them as what they actually are: <strong>MP4 videos<\/strong>.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In this guide, you&#8217;ll learn exactly how to do that \u2014 on any device, in under 30 seconds, for free.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Wait \u2014 Are Reddit GIFs Actually GIFs?<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This is worth understanding before we get into the steps, because it changes how you think about downloading them.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Back in the day, Reddit hosted actual .gif files. They were huge, slow to load, and ate through mobile data. In 2016, Reddit started automatically converting all GIF uploads to MP4 format through their video hosting system, <strong>v.redd.it<\/strong>.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">What this means for you:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>When you <em>watch<\/em> a GIF on Reddit, you&#8217;re actually watching an MP4 video on loop<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>When you try to &#8220;save&#8221; the GIF directly from Reddit, the system gets confused because the file isn&#8217;t a traditional GIF anymore<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>This is why direct saves often fail or produce broken files<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Some older GIFs on Reddit are still hosted on <strong>Imgur<\/strong> (as .gifv files), which is also a video-based format. Same principle applies.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The bottom line: to properly save a Reddit GIF, you need a tool that understands Reddit&#8217;s video infrastructure and pulls the actual MP4 file \u2014 not one that tries to grab a .gif that doesn&#8217;t really exist.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">That tool is <strong><a href=\"https:\/\/rdtvideodownloader.com\/\">RDT Video Downloader<\/a><\/strong>.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Why Download Reddit GIFs as MP4 Instead of GIF?<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Before we get into the steps, here&#8217;s a quick comparison that&#8217;ll make you never want to save actual GIF files again:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th><\/th><th>GIF Format<\/th><th>MP4 Format<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>File size (same clip)<\/td><td>~15\u201340 MB<\/td><td>~1\u20133 MB<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Video quality<\/td><td>Lower, limited colors<\/td><td>Full quality, smooth<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Audio support<\/td><td>\u274c Never<\/td><td>\u2705 Yes<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Compatible with<\/td><td>Most apps<\/td><td>All apps, all devices<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Shareable on WhatsApp\/Instagram<\/td><td>\u26a0\ufe0f Sometimes<\/td><td>\u2705 Always<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Loops<\/td><td>\u2705 Yes<\/td><td>\u2705 Yes (in most players)<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">There is no practical reason to save a Reddit GIF as an actual .gif file. MP4 is smaller, sharper, louder, and more compatible everywhere.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">How to Download Reddit GIFs as MP4 \u2014 Step by Step<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The whole process takes about 20 seconds. Here&#8217;s exactly what to do:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Step 1: Find the Reddit GIF and Copy Its URL<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Open Reddit (in any browser or in the app) and navigate to the GIF post you want to save.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>On desktop:<\/strong> Copy the URL directly from your browser&#8217;s address bar. It&#8217;ll look like: <code>https:\/\/www.reddit.com\/r\/subreddit\/comments\/xxxxxx\/post-title\/<\/code><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>On the Reddit app (iPhone or Android):<\/strong> Tap the <strong>Share<\/strong> button below the post \u2192 tap <strong>Copy Link<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Make sure you&#8217;re copying the link to the <strong>post<\/strong>, not to the GIF file itself. The post URL is what RDT needs to locate and process the file.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Step 2: Go to RDT Video Downloader<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Open a browser and head to <strong><a href=\"https:\/\/rdtvideodownloader.com\/\">rdtvideodownloader.com<\/a><\/strong>.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This free tool works directly in your browser \u2014 no signup, no app download, no Chrome extension required (though one is available if you want even faster downloads \u2014 more on that below).<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Step 3: Paste the URL and Click &#8220;Get Video&#8221;<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Paste the Reddit post URL into the input field on the RDT homepage and hit <strong>Get Video<\/strong>.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">RDT will:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Identify the GIF\/video source (whether it&#8217;s hosted on v.redd.it or Imgur)<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Extract the clean MP4 file<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Prepare it for download in the best available quality<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This typically happens in <strong>1\u20132 seconds<\/strong>.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Step 4: Choose Your Format and Download<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Once processed, you&#8217;ll see download options. For Reddit GIFs, these are usually compact file sizes since GIFs are short clips \u2014 so even the highest quality option won&#8217;t be very large.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Click or tap <strong>Download<\/strong> and the MP4 saves directly to your device:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Windows\/Mac:<\/strong> Saves to your Downloads folder<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Android:<\/strong> Saves to your Downloads folder (accessible in Files app or Gallery)<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>iPhone:<\/strong> See the iPhone-specific section below \u2014 there&#8217;s one extra tap involved<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">How to Save Reddit GIFs on iPhone as MP4<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">iPhone has slightly different behavior for downloads, so here are the exact steps:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Copy the Reddit post URL (Share \u2192 Copy Link in the Reddit app)<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Open <strong>Safari<\/strong> (not Chrome \u2014 Safari works much better for file downloads on iOS)<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Go to <a href=\"https:\/\/rdtvideodownloader.com\/\">rdtvideodownloader.com<\/a><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Paste the URL and tap <strong>Get Video<\/strong><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>When the download button appears, <strong>tap and hold<\/strong> it<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Tap <strong>&#8220;Download Linked File&#8221;<\/strong> from the menu<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>The MP4 saves to your <strong>Files app \u2192 On My iPhone \u2192 Downloads<\/strong><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Want it in your Camera Roll? Open <strong>Files<\/strong>, find the MP4, long-press it, and tap <strong>Share \u2192 Save Video<\/strong>. Done.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">How to Save Reddit GIFs on Android as MP4<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Android is much more straightforward:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Copy the Reddit post URL<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Open Chrome (or any browser) and visit <a href=\"https:\/\/rdtvideodownloader.com\/\">rdtvideodownloader.com<\/a><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Paste the URL and tap <strong>Get Video<\/strong><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Tap <strong>Download<\/strong><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>The MP4 saves to your <strong>Downloads<\/strong> folder<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Open it in any video player or move it to your gallery. That&#8217;s genuinely it.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">How to Download Reddit GIFs from Imgur (.gifv)<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">A lot of older Reddit GIFs are actually hosted on Imgur rather than Reddit&#8217;s own v.redd.it system. You&#8217;ll notice these because the post links out to an Imgur page, and the URL of the actual GIF ends in <strong>.gifv<\/strong>.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The good news: <strong>RDT handles Imgur-hosted GIFs too<\/strong>. You don&#8217;t need to do anything different. Just copy the Reddit post URL (not the Imgur URL) and paste it into RDT. The tool traces back to the source, whether that&#8217;s v.redd.it or Imgur, and grabs the clean MP4.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">If for some reason RDT asks for a direct URL and the GIF is on Imgur, you can also paste the Imgur .gifv URL directly. Just replace <code>.gifv<\/code> with <code>.mp4<\/code> in the URL and paste that into RDT \u2014 Imgur&#8217;s own server will serve you the MP4 version.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">1-Click Reddit GIF Downloads with the RDT Chrome Extension<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">If you&#8217;re on desktop and you find yourself downloading Reddit GIFs regularly, the <strong><a href=\"https:\/\/chromewebstore.google.com\/detail\/rdt-video-downloader-save\/mjphhkbhfkiffmlldcjcapkmninehbej\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">RDT Chrome Extension<\/a><\/strong> will save you a lot of time.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Once installed, a <strong>Download<\/strong> button appears directly on every Reddit GIF and video post \u2014 right inside Reddit&#8217;s interface. You don&#8217;t need to copy URLs or open a new tab. Just scroll, see the GIF you want, click Download.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Can You Download Reddit GIFs with Audio?<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This is a great question and one that trips people up.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Traditional GIF files <strong>never<\/strong> have audio \u2014 the format doesn&#8217;t support it. But since Reddit GIFs are actually MP4 videos, some of them <em>do<\/em> have audio attached, especially if the original uploader added a soundtrack or if the clip came from a video with sound.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">When you download through <strong><a href=\"https:\/\/rdtvideodownloader.com\/\">RDT Video Downloader<\/a><\/strong>, it merges both the audio and video streams from Reddit&#8217;s servers before downloading. So if the original post has audio, your downloaded MP4 will have audio too.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">If you play back your downloaded GIF-MP4 and there&#8217;s no sound, it simply means the original uploader didn&#8217;t include audio \u2014 which is common for pure GIF content.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<blockquote class=\"wp-block-quote is-layout-flow wp-block-quote-is-layout-flow\">\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><\/p>\n<\/blockquote>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What&#8217;s the Best Format to Save Reddit GIFs In?<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Short answer: <strong>MP4<\/strong>.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Longer answer: here&#8217;s how the common options stack up when it comes to Reddit GIFs specifically.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>MP4<\/strong> \u2014 Best overall choice. Small file size, maximum compatibility, supports audio, plays on every device and platform. This is what RDT downloads.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>GIF<\/strong> \u2014 Legacy format. Files are 10\u201320x larger than equivalent MP4s, no audio, limited color depth. Only useful if you specifically need a .gif for a platform that doesn&#8217;t accept video (rare these days).<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>WEBM<\/strong> \u2014 Good quality, small size, but not supported natively on iPhones or in many apps. Not recommended unless you have a specific use case.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>MP4 wins every time<\/strong> for general use. Save the GIF as MP4, and you&#8217;ll never have a compatibility issue.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Common Issues When Downloading Reddit GIFs<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Downloaded file won&#8217;t open<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Make sure it saved as .mp4 and not as a .gifv or incomplete file. Try opening it in VLC media player, which plays virtually any format.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">File downloaded but it&#8217;s silent<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The original GIF probably didn&#8217;t have audio. Play the Reddit post with sound on to confirm. If Reddit plays it silently too, there&#8217;s no audio to save.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">iPhone downloaded a .gifv file instead of MP4<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This can happen if you used Chrome instead of Safari, or if you tapped rather than long-pressed the download button. Repeat the process in Safari and use &#8220;Download Linked File.&#8221;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">RDT can&#8217;t find the video<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The post may be from a private subreddit, or the URL might be incomplete. Try copying the URL again directly from the Reddit post page.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Downloaded GIF looks pixelated<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">You may have selected a lower resolution. Go back and repeat the download, choosing the highest quality option available.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Frequently Asked Questions<\/h2>\n\n\n<style>.kt-accordion-id29_7363e1-d6 .kt-accordion-inner-wrap{column-gap:var(--global-kb-gap-md, 2rem);row-gap:10px;}.kt-accordion-id29_7363e1-d6 .kt-accordion-panel-inner{border-top:0px solid transparent;border-right:1px solid transparent;border-bottom:1px solid transparent;border-left:1px solid transparent;background:#ffffff;padding-top:var(--global-kb-spacing-sm, 1.5rem);padding-right:var(--global-kb-spacing-sm, 1.5rem);padding-bottom:var(--global-kb-spacing-sm, 1.5rem);padding-left:var(--global-kb-spacing-sm, 1.5rem);}.kt-accordion-id29_7363e1-d6 > .kt-accordion-inner-wrap > .wp-block-kadence-pane > .kt-accordion-header-wrap > .kt-blocks-accordion-header{border-top:1px solid #eeeeee;border-right:1p